ditorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#27933644413", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "International cultural organization of countries with turkic populations, speaking languages belonging to the turkic language family Headquartered in Ankara. Founded 1993.", "newValue": "The International Organization of Turkic Culture (TÜRKSOY), established in 1993, serves as a pivotal cultural institution uniting countries with Turkic-speaking populations across various regions, including Central Asia, Eastern Europe, and parts of Siberia. Headquartered in Ankara, Turkey, this organization arose from a collective desire to preserve and promote the rich cultural heritage and linguistic ties of Turkic peoples, making it significant in fostering cultural diplomacy and solidarity among member states, which include Azerbaijan, Kazakhstan, Kyrgyzstan, Uzbekistan, and Turkey.

